---MODULE---
@doc """
Checks if two strings are anagrams of each other.

An anagram is a word or phrase formed by rearranging the letters of a different
word or phrase, typically using all the original letters exactly once.

The function returns false if the strings have different lengths.
Empty strings are considered anagrams of each other.

Time complexity: O(n log n) due to sorting the characters.
"""
@spec are_anagrams(String.t(), String.t()) :: boolean()
def are_anagrams(str1, str2) do
  str1_sorted = String.codepoints(str1) |> Enum.sort()
  str2_sorted = String.codepoints(str2) |> Enum.sort()

  str1_sorted == str2_sorted
end

